{
  "record_id": "013",
  "problem": "Channel additivity violations",
  "collection": "Original research investigation",
  "summary": "A variance about its minimizing mean cannot bound squared deviations about every arbitrary center.",
  "review_status": "source_reviewed",
  "review_note": "No open interpretation blocker was recorded in the preceding source review. This is not a new independent mathematical verification.",
  "original": {
    "excerpt": "For cofactor \\(i\\), pad the magnitude array with zeros to length \\(S_i\\), and let\n\n$$\n\\bar a_i=\\frac{L_i}{S_i}.\n$$\n\nThen\n\n$$\n\\frac{D_i}{S_i}\n=\n\\sum_{\\xi=1}^{S_i}\n\\bigl(|A_i(\\xi)|-\\bar a_i\\bigr)^2,\n\\qquad\nD_i=S_ie_i^2-L_i^2.\n\\tag{6.1}\n$$\n\nRestrict this sum to:\n\n* the \\(G_i\\) surviving unit anchors;\n* the \\(N_i\\) surviving complete opposite-sign pairs.\n\nFor arbitrary \\(\\mu\\in\\mathbb R\\),\n\n$$\n\\frac{D_i}{S_i}\n\\ge\nG_i(1-\\mu)^2\n+\n\\sum_{p=1}^{N_i}\n\\left[\n(r_{p,+}-\\mu)^2+(r_{p,-}-\\mu)^2\n\\right].\n\\tag{6.2}\n$$",
    "context": "D_i=S_i e_i^2-L_i^2 is S_i times the squared-deviation sum about the actual mean bar(a)_i=L_i/S_i. G_i counts retained unit anchors and N_i counts retained opposite-sign pairs with magnitudes r_(p,+),r_(p,-).",
    "locator": "round-55-response.md, lines 577–612"
  },
  "witness": {
    "explanation": "A variance about its minimizing mean cannot bound squared deviations about every arbitrary center.",
    "evidence": "For any nonempty selected coordinate set, the right side of (6.2) grows quadratically as |mu| tends to infinity, whereas D_i/S_i is fixed and finite. As a minimal exact example, one unit coordinate has S_i=L_i=e_i^2=G_i=1 and N_i=0, so D_i/S_i=0; choosing mu=0 makes the asserted right side 1. The valid route evaluates the selected deviations at the actual mean first, then lower-bounds them by their minimum over mu.",
    "scope": "statement_false"
  },
  "archived_witness_excerpt": null,
